\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08EW}{\texttt{Stacks tag 08EW}}


Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces
over $S$. Then $f$ is flat if and only if $f$ is flat at all points of $|X|$.

\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VV}{\texttt{Stacks tag 05VV}}


Let $S$ be a scheme.
Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$.
Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf on $X$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Let $x \in |X|$. We say $\mathcal{F}$ is {\it flat at $x$ over $Y$}
