\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05W0}{\texttt{Stacks tag 05W0}}


If $f$ is unramified at $x$ then $f$ is quasi-finite at $x$.
In particular, an unramified morphism is locally quasi-finite.

\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05W1}{\texttt{Stacks tag 05W1}}


Let $S$ be a scheme.
Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$.
\begin{enumerate}
